WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.580
In an era of information explosion, it is vitally important to develop the ability to think critically and make rational choices.
在信息爆炸的时代，培养批判性思考和理性选择的能力至关重要。

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:20.580
Every day we are flooded with news, advertisements and opinions from countless sources, and not all of them are accurate or well-intentioned.
每天，我们都被来自无数渠道的新闻、广告和观点所淹没，而这些信息并非都准确无误或出于善意。

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.280
Critical thinking helps us separate fact from rumor.
批判性思维帮助我们区分事实与谣言。

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:34.860
Instead of believing everything we read online, we can check where a piece of information comes from, look for evidence and compare different sources before drawing conclusions.
我们不必轻信在网上读到的一切，而可以先查明一条信息来自哪里，寻找证据，并比较不同的来源，然后再下结论。

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.010
Critical thinking also protects us from being misled by advertisements.
批判性思维还能保护我们不被广告误导。

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:51.640
For example, some products claim to be “scientifically proven” without offering any real evidence, and a critical thinker will question such claims rather than buy on impulse.
例如，有些产品声称“经过科学证明”，却拿不出任何真凭实据，而一个善于批判性思考的人会质疑这类说法，而不是一时冲动就购买。

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.230
Equally important is making rational choices.
做出理性的选择同样重要。

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:04.570
When choosing a major, for instance, a wise student weighs interests, abilities and job prospects instead of blindly following the crowd.
比如，在选择专业时，明智的学生会权衡兴趣、能力和就业前景，而不是盲目地随大流。

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:12.870
To develop this ability, students should get into the habit of asking questions such as “Who says so?” and “What is the evidence?”
要培养这种能力，学生应当养成提问的习惯，比如问“谁说的？”和“证据是什么？”

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.300
Schools can also offer courses on logic and media literacy.
学校还可以开设逻辑和媒介素养方面的课程。

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:23.680
With a clear and critical mind, we will no longer be at the mercy of the information around us.
有了清醒而善于批判性思考的头脑，我们就不再任由身边的信息摆布。
